{
    "background_story": "Julien was a talented artist known for his captivating watercolor paintings. However, his creative life was marred by a constant companion - nephralgia, a painful kidney condition that left him with recurring bouts of sharp, stabbing pain. Despite his struggles, Julien refused to let his condition define him. He channeled his emotions into his art, creating breathtaking pieces that reflected his inner turmoil. As his art gained recognition, Julien became an advocate for kidney disease awareness, using his platform to raise funds and support for research. Through his journey, Julien discovered that his nephralgia, though debilitating, had also become a catalyst for his creative expression and a reminder of his resilience.",
